#!/bin/bash
# Stub for systemctl: this container has no init system at all (PID 1 is
# scripts/entrypoint, not systemd or launchd), so there is no real binary to
# wrap the way scripts/npm and scripts/pip3 wrap theirs — this *is* the only
# systemctl in the image.
#
# Exits non-zero, same as a genuinely failing systemctl call, so a caller
# that checks the exit code (or probes `command -v systemctl` before
# assuming success) still behaves correctly — the failure just explains
# itself instead of surfacing as "command not found" or a dbus connection
# error with no context.
cat >&2 <<'EOF'
systemctl: not available — this container has no init system (PID 1 is
vibebox's own entrypoint, not systemd or launchd).

To run something as a persistent background process instead:
  cat /usr/local/share/vibebox/no-systemd.md   (recipe + copy-pasteable template)
  NO_SYSTEMD.md in the execsumo/vibebox repo (same file, rendered on GitHub)

Real examples already in this box: scripts/hermes-gateway, scripts/droid-daemon.
EOF
exit 1
